{
  "version": "1.0",
  "model_version": "kinetics-1.0",
  "note": "Cross-language golden cases for ENGINEERING-CONTRACT section 2.2. Both services/api (pytest) and apps/web (vitest) must pass every case. Protocol parameters are the ones in services/api/app/kinetics/protocols/*.json (copied verbatim to apps/web/src/data/protocols). Compare only the keys present under 'expected'; 'segments' and 'expected_end' are deliberately not asserted. breach_type is the hard_threshold 'label' (or null).",
  "tolerances": {
    "hours": 0.05,
    "fractions": 0.001,
    "degree_hours": 0.05
  },
  "assumptions": [
    "Hard-threshold comparison is strict: max_temp breaches when temp_c > value_c, min_temp when temp_c < value_c.",
    "Readings with taken_at > now are dropped before every step (timeline, confidence, breach).",
    "A reading before harvested_at is clamped so its segment starts at harvested_at.",
    "Confidence: high = >=2 readings and last <= 2 h old; medium = >=1 reading and last <= 8 h old; else low.",
    "Status uses the mid scenario; alerts_crossed lists thresholds [75, 50, 25] with remaining_fraction*100 <= threshold, in that order.",
    "hours_since_last_reading is omitted from 'expected' when there are no readings (implementations may return null)."
  ],
